> I have a table in HTML, and I would like to add a column with a filled in circle, where the color is given by a hex code. How can I do this?
**assistant**:
> You can add a new column to your HTML table and use the CSS `background-color` property to fill a circle with the specified hex color. Here's a basic example of how you can achieve this:
> 
> ```html
> <!DOCTYPE html>
> <html lang="en">
> <head>
>     <meta charset="UTF-8">
>     <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
>     <title>Table with Colored Circles</title>
>     <style>
>         .color-circle {
>             width: 20px;
>             height: 20px;
>             border-radius: 50%;
>             display: inline-block;
>         }
>     </style>
> </head>
> <body>
>     <table border="1">
>         <thead>
>             <tr>
>                 <th>Name</th>
>                 <th>Value</th>
>                 <th>Color</th>
>             </tr>
>         </thead>
>         <tbody>
>             <tr>
>                 <td>Item 1</td>
>                 <td>42</td>
>                 <td><span class="color-circle" style="background-color: #FF5733;"></span></td>
>             </tr>
>             <tr>
>                 <td>Item 2</td>
>                 <td>85</td>
>                 <td><span class="color-circle" style="background-color: #33FF57;"></span></td>
>             </tr>
>             <tr>
>                 <td>Item 3</td>
>                 <td>73</td>
>                 <td><span class="color-circle" style="background-color: #3357FF;"></span></td>
>             </tr>
>         </tbody>
>     </table>
> </body>
> </html>
> ```
> 
> ### Explanation:
> - Each color circle is created using a `<span>` element with a class of `color-circle`.
> - The class `color-circle` is styled with `width`, `height`, and `border-radius: 50%` to make it a circular shape.
> - The `background-color` style is directly applied to each `<span>`, using the hex code for the color you wish to display.
> 
> This approach allows you to dynamically change the color by simply altering the `background-color` style in each row. If you're generating this HTML from a server-side template (like Jinja2) or using JavaScript, you could automate this part of the process. Let me know if you need further assistance!
